	abstract = {Industrialization is the process by which an agrarian and handicraft economy comes to be substituted by an economy in which production is carried out using machine manufacture. Industrialization brought about change not only at the level of the economy, but also of social structure, politics, and culture. Virtually all classical social theorists saw industrialization as a historically disruptive force in British and European society, and also worldwide as European nations exported industrial methods overseas. Deindustrialization refers to the process by which industry comes to play an increasingly smaller role in the structure of the economy owing to the growth of the service sector or the disappearance of industries from national economies as they are trounced by foreign competition or reduced in size owing to technological change.},
